WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.235
-Hi, Kaitlyn!

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:03.937
-Hello, Jimmy!

00:00:03.937 --> 00:00:06.139
-Nice to meet you over Zoom.

00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:08.141
-I know.
It's so nice to meet you.

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:10.276
This is so cool.
This is so cool for me.

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:13.313
I've been a huge fan of yours
for a long time.

00:00:13.313 --> 00:00:14.981
So this is insane.

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:16.849
-This is rad.
I'm a fan of yours as well.

00:00:16.849 --> 00:00:19.051
I know you're busy prepping for

00:00:19.051 --> 00:00:21.254
the film version of
"Dear Evan Hansen."

00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:23.156
-I can't even tell you, Jimmy.

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:26.025
I literally cannot describe
to you how excited I am.

00:00:26.025 --> 00:00:29.895
I think I've only had like
three musical auditions

00:00:29.895 --> 00:00:34.133
in my whole life, and
"Evan Hansen" was one of them.

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:38.571
So it feels insane that I'm
going to be a part of that.

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:40.206
I've always wanted to
do a musical.

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:41.774
-How did the other
two auditions go?

00:00:41.774 --> 00:00:43.375
Not so good?

00:00:43.375 --> 00:00:46.846
-Well, not so good,
but they were okay.

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:51.984
-I had the worst audition ever
in the history of the business.

00:00:51.984 --> 00:00:55.822
I auditioned to be on Broadway
to be Frankenstein.

00:00:55.822 --> 00:00:58.390
-On Broadway?
-Dude, it was --

00:00:58.390 --> 00:01:00.192
I'll never forget it.
Honestly I'm getting --

00:01:00.192 --> 00:01:03.663
I'm about to vomit right now
because I remember going to

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:05.898
an apartment -- I'm not going to
say the casting dir--

00:01:05.898 --> 00:01:09.969
you know, who was casting me,
but the piano player was there,

00:01:09.969 --> 00:01:12.071
and I go, "I'm just going to
sing 'Puttin' on the Ritz.'"

00:01:12.071 --> 00:01:13.839
I go, "Yeah, I can do it."
♪ If you're blue and you ♪

00:01:13.839 --> 00:01:15.341
I go, "Got it."

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:17.176
I get there. They go, "Yeah, we
don't want to hear that song.

00:01:17.176 --> 00:01:18.445
We want to hear this new song."

00:01:18.445 --> 00:01:20.513
I'm like,
"Oh, here's where I get busted

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:22.682
because I'm not
a real actor or a singer."

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:24.617
And it was so bad.

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:27.386
Everyone felt so bad
in the room. It was awful.

00:01:27.386 --> 00:01:29.422
And I remember, I was
so embarrassed when I went home.

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:31.291
It was cold.
It was like December,

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:33.492
and there was steam
coming off of my body.

00:01:33.492 --> 00:01:35.928
[ Laughs ]
That's how embarrassed I was.

00:01:35.928 --> 00:01:38.030
It's like a block of --

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:40.733
-[ Laughs ]
My other musical audition,

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:42.802
that's exactly the same thing
that happened to me.

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:46.339
They're like, "Oh, yeah, no,
you're singing in the wrong key.

00:01:46.339 --> 00:01:49.241
It's actually several keys
higher than what

00:01:49.241 --> 00:01:51.977
you have come in to sing."

00:01:51.977 --> 00:01:55.281
So it was like, "Oh, great,
I don't have that prepared."

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:59.585
-Well, I mean, you're in a band
with your sister Mady.

00:01:59.585 --> 00:02:02.021
And you're called --
Is it Beulahbelle?

00:02:02.021 --> 00:02:04.056
-Yes.

00:02:04.056 --> 00:02:06.225
-You just released
a new song, "Being You."

00:02:06.225 --> 00:02:08.360
I just heard it. It's awesome.

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:11.063
Congrats on that.
-Thanks, Jimmy.

00:02:11.063 --> 00:02:16.101
-But that wasn't your first band
with your sister apparently.

00:02:16.101 --> 00:02:18.971
-It was not.
-Yeah.

00:02:18.971 --> 00:02:27.479
-We used to be called Hot Pink,
which I think is a great name,

00:02:27.479 --> 00:02:30.082
and I don't know
why we changed it.

00:02:30.082 --> 00:02:34.220
-This is bizarre, but we
actually talked to some people

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:35.921
and we actually
got some unseen footage

00:02:35.921 --> 00:02:37.757
from an early performance
of yours.

00:02:37.757 --> 00:02:41.227
This is -- Check out you on
guitar. This is pretty awesome.

00:02:41.227 --> 00:02:42.862 line:0%
♪♪

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:43.996
Oh, my gosh.

00:02:43.996 --> 00:02:50.536 line:0%
♪♪

00:02:50.536 --> 00:02:52.272
-Oh, my gosh!

00:02:52.272 --> 00:02:56.775
-The commitment I had to -- I
think I remember telling myself,

00:02:56.775 --> 00:02:59.645
"I need to get down on my knees
and really get into it,"

00:02:59.645 --> 00:03:01.247
and then I quickly got up.

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:02.648
I was not down on the ground.

00:03:02.648 --> 00:03:04.317
[ Laughing ] I got up so fast.

00:03:04.317 --> 00:03:07.186
-You rocked. That is one
of the coolest things.

00:03:07.186 --> 00:03:08.955
Hey, I want to talk
about your projects

00:03:08.955 --> 00:03:11.257
because you have so many
besides "Dear Evan Hansen."

00:03:11.257 --> 00:03:14.627
You have a movie out now
on HBO and HBO Max

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:16.529
called "Coastal Elites."

00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:18.297
How did you get
involved with that?

00:03:18.297 --> 00:03:22.034
-I got a call from Jay Roach,
who's the director,

00:03:22.034 --> 00:03:24.403
and sent me the script,
and he asked me

00:03:24.403 --> 00:03:26.706
to play the role of the nurse.

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:29.275
So, there's five separate
monologues of all of

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:32.211
these different characters
sort of, like, talking about

00:03:32.211 --> 00:03:35.047
their frustration about
the current state of the world,

00:03:35.047 --> 00:03:39.785
and he asked me to be in it
with Bette and Dan Levy

00:03:39.785 --> 00:03:42.889
and Sarah Paulson and Issa,
and I was just sort of like,

00:03:42.889 --> 00:03:46.326
"Are you sure?
This is a lot of pressure."

00:03:46.326 --> 00:03:48.061
But it was really incredible

00:03:48.061 --> 00:03:51.130
to be able to shoot something
in quarantine. It was wild.

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:53.566
-It's really a cool thing
to watch. It's great.

00:03:53.566 --> 00:03:56.201
You also have a new series
on Hulu called "Monsterland."

00:03:56.201 --> 00:03:57.937
It premieres tomorrow.

00:03:57.937 --> 00:04:01.240
How would you describe this one?

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:06.012
-Yeah, "Monsterland" sort of
follows several characters

00:04:06.012 --> 00:04:10.816
that are -- we follow sort of
these broken and troubled people

00:04:10.816 --> 00:04:16.088
who are forced to sort of
cope with the darkest parts

00:04:16.088 --> 00:04:19.258
of themselves, and I play
a young girl named Toni

00:04:19.258 --> 00:04:22.061
who is a mother
to a 4-year-old girl.

00:04:22.061 --> 00:04:25.298
And she is also trying to
cope with just, you know --

00:04:25.298 --> 00:04:27.132
my character is
just trying to cope with

00:04:27.132 --> 00:04:29.035
her inner monster as well,

00:04:29.035 --> 00:04:34.440
and it was the first time I have
ever played a mom in my life.

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:40.647
And it was also the first time
I did a Cajun French accent,

00:04:40.647 --> 00:04:44.383
which is as difficult
as it sounds.

00:04:44.383 --> 00:04:46.885
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:04:46.885 --> 00:04:49.054
-Well, you knocked it out of
the park. I want to show a clip.

00:04:49.054 --> 00:04:51.557
Here's Kaitlyn Dever
in "Monsterland."

00:04:51.557 --> 00:04:52.958
Take a look at this.

00:04:52.958 --> 00:04:54.359
-My name is Alex.

00:04:54.359 --> 00:04:56.262
-Where you from, Alex?

00:04:56.262 --> 00:04:59.398
-Uh, nearby.

00:04:59.398 --> 00:05:01.967
-You lyin' already.

00:05:01.967 --> 00:05:03.803
-Why do you assume
that I'm lying?

00:05:08.474 --> 00:05:10.375
-Cause you ain't talkin' flat.

00:05:10.375 --> 00:05:12.511
Folks around here sound like
they filed the letter G

00:05:12.511 --> 00:05:14.380
from the damn alphabet.

00:05:18.617 --> 00:05:20.185
-I'm here doing a job.

00:05:20.185 --> 00:05:21.754
-Offshore?
-Mm-hmm.

00:05:21.754 --> 00:05:24.290
-Then you better heal up
and get a straight story

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:26.325
'cause trouble
don't make pay date.

00:05:26.325 --> 00:05:29.328
-Well...

00:05:29.328 --> 00:05:30.863
I'm no trouble.

00:05:30.863 --> 00:05:33.032
-Yeah,
and I'm the Queen of Sheba.

00:05:33.032 --> 00:05:34.633
-My thanks to Kaitlyn Dever.

00:05:34.633 --> 00:05:37.804
"Coastal Elites" is
on HBO and HBO Max now.

00:05:37.804 --> 00:05:40.740
And "Monsterland" premieres
on Hulu tomorrow.

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:42.507
Thank you so much again
for coming on, Kaitlyn.

00:05:42.507 --> 00:05:44.344
I appreciate it.
-Thank you, Jimmy.

00:05:44.344 --> 00:05:45.912
Thanks for having me.
This was awesome.

